Jukka Lahtinen wrote on 07/17/2003 09:40 AM:

[various things which would be cool to have with bones files]

There are yet more interesting ways to increase fun & compatibility. One
that I have thought about for some time is integrating functionality
within bones files. The problem is--this is very incompatible with the
current nethack. Also from the style aspect it will be a wholly
different game, I know:)

But wouldn't it be nifty to have a patch that adds say the pink unicorn
horn which has the function of making you hallucinate if cursed and
temporary increasing charisma when not. This functionality would also be
added to any saved bones which the patched game produces and this tool
could be used even within unpatched versions. (All the patch would do to
the game is actually just registering the new object with the games
object system.)

Yes one would need to write that object handling system--perhaps
something like an integrated script compiler with the language providing
hooks for actions (like apply) and passive stuff like (got_blinded) so
all current functionality could be mimicked. This smells pretty much
like object-orientedness is needed but it need not be if thought out
carefully. And of course there would be huge opportunities for abuse, so
perhaps some public key signing system for objects could be employed,
lest ppl end up downloading 3d100 weapons from bones-sharing programmes
and thus spoiling their games....

Ok this is probably not a concept for nethack as it is--it would change
the game too much. Nevertheless I think it could provide some very fun
gameplay.

